+# Todo due date (Fälligkeitsdatum) Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional due date (`dueDate`, `JJJJ-MM-TT`); the API computes `overdue` (not done AND dueDate before today UTC) on every todo response and supports `GET /todos?overdue=true`; the list page shows the date next to the title, an „überfällig" label, and a „nur überfällige" toggle.
+
+**Architecture:** `src/store.mjs` validates and stores `dueDate`; `src/app.mjs` computes `overdue` at serialization time against UTC today and applies the `?overdue=true` filter; `public/index.html` renders date/label/toggle and refetches with the query param. One source of truth for „today" lives server-side.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24 builtins only (`node:http`, `node:test`), zero dependencies; vanilla JS module in the list page.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-01-todo-due-date-design.md` (Ticket #1, posted as Approved Spec comment on the ticket)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` and map to HTTP 400.
+- TDD: write a failing test in `test/` first, then implement.
+- Every new UI element carries a `data-testid` (`todo-due`, `todo-overdue`, `overdue-only`).
+- UI copy in German; no styling changes.
+- Branch `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`, base `main`; PR opened as draft (`WIP: 1: Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos`).
+- End-to-end verification by the agent in the running app via Playwright (per AGENTS.md), screenshots saved outside the repo.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- `2026-02-30` must be rejected with 400 (strict format + real calendar date) — Task 1.
+- „Today" is UTC: a dueDate of yesterday UTC is overdue even if local time is still today — Task 2.
+- A done todo with a past dueDate is never overdue and never in the filtered list — Task 2.
+- A todo without dueDate is never overdue and stays in the unfiltered list — Tasks 1–2.
+- `PATCH { "dueDate": null }` removes the date; `overdue` becomes `false` afterwards — Tasks 1–2.
+- `?overdue=` with any value other than exactly `true` returns the full list — Task 2.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — `dueDate` validation and storage
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: nothing new (HTTP layer already passes bodies to `store.add` / `store.update`).
+- Produces: `store.add({ title, dueDate? })` → `{ id, title, done, dueDate }` with `dueDate` default `null`; `store.update(id, { dueDate })` accepts a valid date string or `null` (removes). Invalid values throw `ValidationError`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests** in `test/app.test.mjs`:
+  - `POST /todos` with `{ title: 'A', dueDate: '2026-12-24' }` → 201 and body `dueDate === '2026-12-24'`, `done === false`.
+  - `POST /todos` with `dueDate: '2026-02-30'` → 400; `'2026-13-01'` → 400; `'2026-11-05T10:00:00'` → 400; `dueDate: 42` → 400.
+  - `PATCH /todos/1` with `{ dueDate: '2027-01-01' }` → 200, `dueDate === '2027-01-01'`; with `{ dueDate: null }` → 200, `dueDate === null`; with `{ dueDate: 'gestern' }` → 400.
+  - Update the existing `creates and lists todos` test: expected list is now `[{ id: 1, title: 'Milch kaufen', done: false, dueDate: null }]`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run `npm test` — the new tests fail** (dueDate is dropped / not validated).
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `src/store.mjs`:** private `parseDueDate(value)` helper — `undefined`/`null` → `null`; a string must match `/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/` AND round-trip through `Date.UTC` (rejects `2026-02-30`), else throw `ValidationError('dueDate must be a YYYY-MM-DD date or null')`. Use it in `add` (default `null`) and in `update` when `'dueDate' in patch`.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run `npm test` — all tests pass.**
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** (`git add src/store.mjs test/app.test.mjs && git commit -m "feat: store dueDate with strict YYYY-MM-DD validation"`).
+
+### Task 2: API — computed `overdue` field and `?overdue=true` filter
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/app.mjs`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs`
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `store.list()`, `store.get(id)`, `store.add(...)`, `store.update(...)` (raw todos with `dueDate`).
+- Produces: every todo JSON response (GET `/todos`, GET `/todos/:id`, POST `/todos`, PATCH `/todos/:id`) is the todo plus `overdue: boolean`; `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only overdue todos.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Write the failing tests** in `test/app.test.mjs`. Use UTC-relative dates: `const day = 86400000; const iso = (d) => new Date(d).toISOString().slice(0, 10); const today = iso(Date.now()); const yesterday = iso(Date.now() - day); const tomorrow = iso(Date.now() + day);`
+  - Create four todos: `{ title: 'past', dueDate: yesterday }`, `{ title: 'today', dueDate: today }`, `{ title: 'future', dueDate: tomorrow }`, `{ title: 'none' }`, plus `PATCH` the `past` one to `done: true` in a second server, or simpler: create five and mark one done.
+  - `GET /todos` → `overdue` flags: past=`true` (when not done), today=`false`, future=`false`, none=`false`; after `PATCH {done:true}` on past → `overdue === false`.
+  - `GET /todos?overdue=true` → exactly the not-done past todo(s); `GET /todos?overdue=false` and `GET /todos?overdue=1` → full list.
+  - `GET /todos/:id` → includes `overdue`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run `npm test` — the new tests fail** (no `overdue`, no filter).
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `src/app.mjs`:** `const todayUtc = () => new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);` and `const withOverdue = (todo) => ({ ...todo, overdue: !todo.done && todo.dueDate !== null && todo.dueDate < todayUtc() });` Apply in the four response sites; in `GET /todos`, filter `url.searchParams.get('overdue') === 'true'` before mapping.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run `npm test` — all tests pass.**
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** (`git commit -m "feat: compute overdue (UTC) in API responses and add ?overdue=true filter"`).
+
+### Task 3: List page — date, „überfällig" label, „nur überfällige" toggle
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `public/index.html`
+- Test: `test/app.test.mjs` (markup assertions)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: `GET /todos` and `GET /todos?overdue=true` (todos with `dueDate`, `overdue`).
+- Produces: rendered list; new elements carry `data-testid="todo-due"`, `data-testid="todo-overdue"`, `data-testid="overdue-only"`.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Extend the `serves the list page` test** in `test/app.test.mjs`: `GET /` body matches `/data-testid="overdue-only"/` and contains `todo-due` and `todo-overdue`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Run `npm test` — fails** (markup missing).
+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement in `public/index.html`:** keep the existing render loop, but render per todo: `todo-title` span (title + ` ✓` when done), `todo-due` span with `todo.dueDate ?? ''`, and a `todo-overdue` span with text `überfällig` only when `todo.overdue`. Add a checkbox/label „nur überfällige" with `data-testid="overdue-only"` whose change re-fetches (`/todos?overdue=true` when checked, else `/todos`) and re-renders.
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run `npm test` — all tests pass.**
+- [ ] **Step 5: Commit** (`git commit -m "feat: show due date, overdue label and overdue-only toggle on the list page"`).
+
+### Task 4: End-to-end verification and integration
+
+**Files:** none (verification only); then git/Gitea operations.
+
+- [ ] **Step 1: Start the app** — `PORT=3000 npm start &` from the repo root; wait for `GET http://localhost:3000/health` → `{"ok":true}`.
+- [ ] **Step 2: Drive the UI with Playwright** (per AGENTS.md): load `http://localhost:3000/`; create via API (`POST /todos`) todos with yesterday/today/no due date and verify on the page: `todo-due` shows the date, `todo-overdue` shows „überfällig" only on the past one; toggle `overdue-only` and verify only the overdue todo remains; save screenshots outside the repo (e.g. `/tmp/opencode/`).
+- [ ] **Step 3: Shut the app down** (kill the background `npm start`).
+- [ ] **Step 4: Run `npm test` once more, then push** `git push -u origin 1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`.
+- [ ] **Step 5: Open the draft PR** per `.agents/includes/ticketing.md`: `tea pulls create --login "e2e" --repo adw/demo-todo --base main --head 1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos --title "WIP: 1: Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos" --description "<implementation summary + ticket reference #1>"`.
+- [ ] **Step 6: Close-out on the ticket:** post the `Implementation Summary` and the `Cost Summary` (per `.agents/includes/cost.md`) as comments on issue 1 and move it to `status:review`. Never close it, never publish the PR.
